  "id": "Compound::DB00129 - Gene::6542",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between L-ornithine and Slc7a2, mediated through the protein Slc7a3. L-ornithine binds to Slc7a3, which is involved in the transport of various amino acids across cellular membranes. This involvement is further supported by the fact that Slc7a3 participates in the transport of L-lysine, arginine, and basic amino acids, all of which are transported by Slc7a2. The shared involvement of Slc7a3 in the transport of different amino acids implies a functional overlap between Slc7a3 and Slc7a2, potentially through a common mechanism of amino acid transport. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a robust connection between L-ornithine and Slc7a2, likely through the regulation of amino acid transporters. The mechanism appears to involve the binding of L-ornithine to Slc7a3, which then facilitates the transport of amino acids, possibly through a shared functional pathway with Slc7a2.",
